      "message": "IIUC, calling this will actually mutate the state in IpSecService ? If so that doesn\u0027t look like a very reasonable way to design it because it is very counter-intuitive action at a distance. Besides, if the caller forgets to call applyTunnelModeTransform, will this cause leaks in the system server ?\n\nISTM it would be better to produce a new object that encapsulates the information needed by the desired migration. This could be an IpSecTransform object (possibly returned by a method like this one, but preferably simply created from the Builder), or it could be a separate object to pass to a new method in IpSecManager.\n\nAlso, only remotely related : do we intend to eventually expose tunnel mode publicly ? It looks like it would be generally useful.",
